Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||09-16-2001||07:43 PM||||well.. the rear engine trunk compartment or whatever its called  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> i'm just wondering how hot it gets in there. I dont plan on bringing home ice cream in it... ok... i'll admit it, i want to put an amplifier back there but wonder if its too hot for the amp.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||09-16-2001||10:51 PM||||It does get hot!!!!! The other problem is that there is no air circulation!!! The trunk compartment is sealed?<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||09-17-2001||01:57 AM||||I was thinking of putting a CD changer back there but thought again. It would make sense that it gets hot, even thought it is sealed. The point being that there is in fact NO circulation because it is sealed.<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hippocrat||09-17-2001||02:06 AM||||good place for an amp is in the front compartment. can build it onto a hinged platform and still have storage room .. cd changers look ok mounted on the ceiling by the break light. easily accessible to.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jefrysuko||09-17-2001||02:07 AM||||I have been toying with the idea of making the fan in the passenger corner of the trunk blow air into the trunk.  I think orge has a writeup of how to control that fan with a separate thermostat which you could mount in the trunk.  Then you would just have to cut a vent somewhere.  I had thought venting into the taillights would be a good idea.<P>Hmmm.  I might just have to do that.||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||09-17-2001||02:53 AM||||I have my amp (300 Watt bridged) and crossover mounted on a board behind the driver's seat.  I'm 5'10", and I have the seat at the second to last notch on the tracks.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||DKOV||09-17-2001||12:43 PM||||Let me get this straight...  You are all wondering HOW it gets warm in the trunk?  How HEAT from a REAR ENGINE car that positions the EXHAUST right up against the trunk comparment gets hot?<P>I MUST be reading this wrong  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000007||fieronv||09-17-2001||03:10 PM||||<BR> There are many factors on how hot the trunk gets.<BR>1. what engiine you have.<BR>2. what color is your car.<BR>3. where you are located (ambeint air temp).<P>On average with out using a thermal coupler I would say the temp gets up to 125 degrees F.<BR>As for putting an Amp in there the concern I would have isn't temp but length of speaker wires and rca to the amp. I have my CD changer in the trunk and have never had a problem with heat. I live in Nevada and have a black car. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2_WEB_1.jpg">   <BR>85GT (twoloud)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fieronv (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||AusFiero||09-18-2001||08:53 AM||||I have 2 amps mounted in my trunk. Not a problem to date.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
